        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_53a81aee1231436a9e96ab7aa4dfede8",
      "statement": "A Word (.docx) upload is planned into pages via planDocxPages (lib/identify/docxPages.ts) before extraction, because a .docx schedule may contain page-image screenshots, inline table text, or a mix of both shapes.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/api/upload/route.ts#L122-L155",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b39f6fe8a33b43cea99f6d8415a97cafb46b5f5fcec4eaa9e1af8b1ddf621a1e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f6ee82dc982a4a5ba51735088be9cdd0",
      "statement": "The browser-prepared multi-page upload path exists to work around Vercel's 4.5 MB request-body limit enforced at the platform edge before the route runs, which otherwise surfaces to the estimator as an undiagnosable 'Failed to fetch'.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/api/upload/route.ts#L17-L29",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:18532609db30037f8239fd099475ec52c67b97dad9e988c5ad000740446e19a8:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/prepareUpload.ts#L9-L25",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9307a2cd3b6ab37822fe7033128dcc81bc9198003daafb3bd403a940d429bf21:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e9d984ddd51049a195452af226f64691",
      "statement": "app/prepareUpload.ts's prepareWordUpload re-encodes each embedded page image from a Word schedule as JPEG scaled to at most 1568px on the long edge (the vision API's own downsample threshold) using a descending JPEG-quality ladder, and posts the pages as separate multipart parts to stay under Vercel's body limit.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/prepareUpload.ts#L59-L63",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:49cd5ed61c94ef956e1590bb1284b912a32bd78902b6de15a45e82191df4d1e2:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/prepareUpload.ts#L95-L198",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7d68291bb20b77a1d04f3f5a6d0a8c7b636313f244ba0ffebb2491536b91dc95:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ea4f31e851f54a48afd9ab484c1a9f2f",
      "statement": "prepareWordUpload returns null (signaling 'upload the raw .docx') when the document has no embedded page images or when it contains literal table rows, since this browser-side path can only carry page images and would silently drop table content; the API route's own .docx reader handles those shapes directly. It throws instead of submitting an oversized request when no quality step brings the document under the upload budget.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/prepareUpload.ts#L133-L198",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:68cdd005ab7ae13db9f9d3b6d1d20e442589fc77e34d218605da4dae12a9fda3:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_773d0e4bdfac4587ae8adacc75005b7c",
      "statement": "POST /api/upload's response source field is 'pdf' whenever the document was read by Claude (PDF, image, or Word alike) and 'sheet' for the known-column workbook parser path; this is a fixed route-contract value, not a literal file-type indicator.",
